UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventhistoryonthedouble23691-20260523@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261015T144959Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260523
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261026
SUMMARY:History on the Double
DESCRIPTION:Two decks\, one timeline\, and absolutely no sense of direction. Good morning\, historians\, adventurers\, and anyone who got on the wrong bus but is too polite to admit it! Prepare yourself for an extraordinary expedition aboard our towering yellow vintage London double-decker bus\, now thundering proudly through the streets of Downtown Frederick\, Maryland. You’ll start your day along the scenic Carroll Creek Park\, where our gleaming double-decker waits like a massive custard-colored teapot on wheels. Once aboard\, take your seat\, clutch your belongings\, and abandon all responsibility\, our Clippies will handle the chaos from here. As we trundle through historic Downtown Frederick\, you’ll be treated to a fully guided Frederick history tour through centuries of local stories\, from colonial shenanigans to architectural brilliance\, from Civil War-era landmarks to the occasional ghost who refuses to pay rent. Perfect for families\, visitors\, history lovers\, and anyone looking for fun things to do in Frederick Maryland\, this unforgettable historical sightseeing tour is your front-row seat to the city’s remarkable past\, served with a generous helping of British wit.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/history-on-the-double/23691/
END:VEVENT
