BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventjumbospumpkinpatchfallfestival11483-20261016@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261015T144959Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261016
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261017
SUMMARY:Jumbo's Pumpkin Patch Fall Festival
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the season with a full day of festive fun for all ages at Jumbo’s Pumpkin Patch! From classic farm adventures to fall-themed attractions\, our Fall Fun Festival is the perfect weekend outing for families\, friends\, and pumpkin lovers. What’s Included with Admission: Your ticket includes unlimited access to a variety of seasonal attractions: Hayrides through the farm 30+ acre u-pick pumpkin patch (pumpkins sold by the pound) Corn maze (14 acres) Petting zoo Jumping pillow Giant slides Mini mazes for younger guests Playgrounds and yard games General Store with fall shopping and décor​ Optional Add-Ons: (Available for Purchase Onsite - Saturday and Sunday Only) Enhance your day with these fun extras: Pony Rides – $7 Face Painting – $4 Sandy Candy (Edible Sand Art) – $4 Corn Cannon – $5 (3 shots) ​ Food & Drinks: Come hungry! A variety of food\, snacks\, and beverages are available for purchase\, including selections from Liquidity Ale Works of Mt. Airy. Tickets available online or at the gate.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/jumbos-pumpkin-patch-fall-festival/11483/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventmidnightmargaritasa212bafterdarkexperience26165-20261016@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261015T144959Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261016
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261017
SUMMARY:Midnight Margaritas - A 21+ After Dark Experience
DESCRIPTION:Calling all witches\, warlocks\, wild hearts\, and lovers of a little midnight madness! Midnight Margaritas presented by Frederick Keys Special Events in partnership with Warehouse Cinemas is a one-of-a-kind 21+ late-night experience at the Keys Stadium\, inspired by the beloved world of Practical Magic . Grab your broom\, gather your coven\, and prepare for a magical night under the moon! Gates open at 8:00 PM\, with early access to Suite Guests beginning at 7:00 PM. The evening begins with a live band playing all your favorite covers from Fleetwood Mac to '70s rock-inspired hits before the night takes a wicked turn with a witchy\, Halloween-inspired DJ dance party. We're transforming the 3rd Base Coors Light Tent into the ultimate late-night dance floor and lounge. As the clock strikes twelve\, raise your glass for a Midnight Margarita Toast. Explore The Moon Market\, featuring a spooky collection of unique vendors\, special items available for purchase\, and complimentary crafty activities throughout the evening. Sip your way through the stadium with specialty margarita offerings and late-night concession bites for purchase. Keep an eye out for a little extra magic from our roaming entertainment. VIP guests can enjoy access to a special all-you-can-eat tacos\, included with their ticket\, as well as a Three Margarita Flight. Costumes and witchy attire are strongly encouraged. So put on your best black dress\, grab your broomstick\, and join us for a night filled with music\, margaritas\, magic\, and a little midnight mischief. This is a 21+ Event. Valid IDs will be checked upon entry. All guests must be 21 years of age or older to attend Midnight Margaritas. You will be denied access regardless of ticket if you can not present valid ID. This event is RAIN OR SHINE. Musical performances and activities are taking place under cover. There are parts of the event that are not under cover and in the case of inclement weather please dress appropriately. Event would only be canceled in the case of extreme or unsafe weather. All communications about weather are made via email and social media.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/midnight-margaritas-a-21%2b-after-dark-experience/26165/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventparkavenuebandliveinconcertatrockwellbrewery1016267pm26214-20261016@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261015T144959Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261016
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261017
SUMMARY:PARK AVENUE BAND Live in Concert at Rockwell Brewery 10/16/26 7PM
DESCRIPTION:They are Finally Back!! Frederick's own PARK AVENUE BAND hits the Rockwell stage Friday 10/16/26 at 7PM to get you up and on the dance floor! Be sure to bring your dancing shoes! Come out and enjoy incredible vocals and the hottest horn sound in the area! Performing throughout the Mid-Atlantic area and beyond. This ultimate party band features a wide variety of Classic Rock and Funk favorites\, especially rockin' dance tunes that's definitely going to get everyone moving\, dancing and singing along. Exceptional musicianship and vocal skills put Park Avenue in a class of their own when it comes to live performance. The band's experience and versatility allow for a large and diverse repertoire\; AND requests are welcome! This is definitely a band that you're going to want to see live! Grab all of your friends and get to the Brewery early to grab a cocktail and get near the dance floor! COVER CHARGE AT THE DOOR. 100% goes to the band!
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/park-avenue-band-live-in-concert-at-rockwell-brewery-10-16-26-7pm/26214/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventthetombloodduo26205-20261016@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261015T144959Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261016
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261017
SUMMARY:The Tom Blood Duo
DESCRIPTION:Your Friday night just got better… Join us at Sandbox Brewhouse as The Tom Blood Duo takes over our stage! Featuring seasoned musicians Tom Blood and Chris Marsh\, this dynamic duo is bringing a versatile setlist of acoustic classic rock favorites for the perfect evening soundtrack.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/the-tom-blood-duo/26205/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventtrailofjackolanternswithtrickortreating9284-20261016@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261015T144959Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261016
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Trail of Jack-O-Lanterns with Trick or Treating
DESCRIPTION:Looking for something fun to do with the children this October that won’t scare them and is appropriate for any age? You found it! Join us 6pm to 10pm for our walking Trail of Jack-O-Lanterns. Admission is $16.00\, credit only ages 2 and older (babies are free) & includes our Trail\, fire pits\, and our Animal Barn (open 6pm to 9:00pm.) to see your furry friends. Admission will also include trick or treating for children from 7pm to 8pm. The Trail closes at 9pm. Bring your children (and your adults) in costume to add to the fun! Available for purchase will be night hayrides\, pumpkin flashlights\, Trick or Treat bags\, glow necklaces\, and more! Gates open 5:30pm. Last admission is 8:30pm. Check our website for NEW nightly specials! Dates: Oct 16\, 17\, 18\, 23\, 24\, 25\, 30 and 31\, 2026 (weather permitting) NOTE: The Trail is a separate event from our daytime petting farm and requires a separate\, new admission to enter.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/trail-of-jack-o-lanterns-with-trick-or-treating/9284/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventtrekortreat21019-20261016@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261015T144959Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261016
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Trek or Treat
DESCRIPTION:Get off the screen and into the scream at Tree Trekkers for Trek or Treat! It’s trick or treat in the trees! This Halloween\, the forest transforms into a treetop adventure full of tricks\, treats\, and thrills. Climb\, zip\, and creep your way through the trails as candy stations await in the canopy. Bigfoot’s lurking in the woods… but don’t worry\, he’s just here for the candy! Landing zones are sponsored by our favorite local businesses with treats that will delight not fright! Costumes encouraged! (Make sure we can still harness you though!) Prizes for best dressed trekkers! A spooktacular adventure for all ages 4+ (4 -7 year olds will need to climb with an adult) Trek or Treat bag is included with Trek or Treat Ticket. $7 Trek or Treat add on bags available for Little-foot combo tickets\, gift voucher redemptions\, and groups. (Call to book 301-888-8735) Trek or Treat bags can also be purchased for younger siblings who want to trick or treat on our ground pathway sponsored by our local non-profits. Includes access to all 16 Timber Trek Trails Climbers will begin their adventure in ground school\, advancing to the bunny slope trails where they will need to show competency with their equipment and a firm understanding of the course rules before advancing to the main platform. Gloves are highly recommended\, but not required. Guests can bring their own full-finger climbing gloves or purchase gloves if they choose. This is a self guided adventure recommended for ages 8+ (4-7 year olds require an adult climber to climb with them and will be required to start on our purple trails) Participants will need to be 4ft or taller to go on our Red Zipline Trails Weight Limit: 30-250lbs Everyone on the property will need to sign a waiver. (This includes climbers and spectators) Must wear closed toed/closed heeled shoes\, such as sneakers or boots\, no crocs\, sandals\, or backless footwear. If you do not see a time or date available that works with your schedule please call 301-888-8735 or email INFO@TREETREKKERSMD.COM TREK OR TREAT DATES: 10/16\, 10/17\, 10/23\, 10/24\, 10/30\, 10/31 (ONLY TREK OR TREAT TICKETS ARE AVAILABLE ON THOSE DATES) TREK OR TREAT
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/trek-or-treat/21019/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgevent2026exhibitsatmuseumoffrederickcountyhistory24908-20261017@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261015T144959Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261017
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261018
SUMMARY:2026 Exhibits at Museum of Frederick County History
DESCRIPTION:Take a deep dive into various topics that have defined Frederick's history\, as we celebrate America's 250th anniversary and our County's role in the Revolution. Featuring brand new exhibits: Cultivating Independence: Frederick in the Revolution Witnessing Revolution All Saints Street: Avenue to the History of Frederick and Its African American Community Growing Gold: A History of Frederick’s Goldfish Industry And returning favorites: Etchison Connections Timeless Toys 24 E Church Street Decorative Arts See our all new and renovated exhibits\, March 7\,2026 through December 12\, 2026. Buy tickets here.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/2026-exhibits-at-museum-of-frederick-county-history/24908/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventalleynights23158-20261017@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261015T144959Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261017
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261018
SUMMARY:Alley Nights
DESCRIPTION:Welcome to Alley Nights — your Saturday night destination in Downtown Frederick. With three bars open\, the party moves wherever the night takes you! Start in our newly renovated Main Bar\, catch the DJ spinning in Terrace\, or head upstairs to the rooftop bar for drinks and views of downtown Frederick. Add late-night bites\, great music\, and a lively crowd — and you’ve got everything you need for the perfect Saturday night! Benefactor Events joins us every first and third Saturday of the month to get the party going in Terrace! Meet us at Alley Nights! No cover | 21+ event.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/alley-nights/23158/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventbarksbrews26boos26080-20261017@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261015T144959Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261017
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261018
SUMMARY:Barks\, Brews\, & Boos
DESCRIPTION:We have partnered with Monocacy Brewing Company to bring you an afternoon of spooky fun for your families and furbabies alike - join us for fabulous beer\, Howl-O-Ween carnival games\, a silent auction\, and an all-around beautiful fall day perusing our vendor stalls and enjoying the brewery. Each ticket includes a complimentary serving of beer\, a commemorative koozie\, an entry into our door prize raffle\, a ticket for one Howl-O-Ween carnival game\, and unlimited access to our other activities and vendors. Costumes- human and canine- are of course welcomed! Online ticket sales end October 16th\, but day-of tickets will be available at the venue and are $30. The first 100 people to buy tickets will receive a pawsome gift bag stuffed with lots of goodies! We are a totally volunteer-run organization so 100% of proceeds directly benefit our rescue animals! Visit us at awlfc.org for more details on our mission and impact.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/barks-brews-%26-boos/26080/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:httpswwwvisitfrederickorgeventexhibitopeningwherelightsettles3awalterbartmanranageralis26nathanielwilliams26244-20261017@visitfrederick
DTSTAMP:20261015T144959Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261017
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261018
SUMMARY:Exhibit Opening - Where Light Settles: Walter Bartman\, Rana Geralis\, & Nathaniel Williams
DESCRIPTION:Three nationally recognized\, highly regarded painters will be at the gallery to discuss their work and process and to answer questions for this special exhibition featuring new paintings. All three painters were recently featured in the September and October issues of American Art Collector Magazine\, through their representation at Lockhouse Gallery. Walter Bartman founded the Yellow Barn Studio in Glen Echo\, Maryland where he is currently the director. He has mentored and taught thousands of accomplished painters. He paints in plein air\, particularly around Frederick County\, near his home studio. His work is kept in national and international collections. Rana Geralis is a plein air landscape painter and also specializes in equine subjects. She is a master of the palette knife\, which allows for thick\, vibrant applications of paint in her work. Rana participates in many plein air competitions and has won numerous awards in the field. She also teaches painting at the Yellow Barn Studio. Nathaniel Williams is a well-known American Realism painter who is represented nationally through galleries\, shows\, and museums. He paints local scenes in Brunswick and Frederick County areas. His work has gained major popularity at the Affordable Art Fair in Chelsea\, New York City. Don't miss this opportunity to hear their process and ask them questions!! Light Food\, Wine\, and Beverages will be served. This is a casual and free event.
URL:https://www.visitfrederick.org/event/exhibit-opening-where-light-settles%3a-walter-bartman-rana-geralis-%26-nathaniel-williams/26244/
END:VEVENT
